No, remoteEntry.js and remote.d.ts are two different files with different purposes in Module Federation.
1. remoteEntry.js — runtime file
In your products/vite.config.ts:
federation({
  name: 'products',
  filename: 'remoteEntry.js',
  exposes: {
    './ProductList': './src/App.tsx',
  },
})


- remoteEntry.js is generated by the Module Federation plugin.
- It exposes the Products microfrontend to the host at runtime.
- The host loads it using a URL such as http://localhost:3001/remoteEntry.js.
2. remote.d.ts — TypeScript declaration file
Your declaration file tells TypeScript how to understand remote modules when you import them into the host.
For example, in host/src/remote.d.ts



